lid RPC response time threshold value","nsx.node.tunnel.active":"Total Active Tunnels","rule.audit.logs.no.rule.executed":"No rule executed in the past 7 days.","pdf.table.heading.steps":"Steps*","lightsail.instance.statecode":"Instance State Code","practice.instance.idle.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>An instance is deemed to be idle, by analyzing CloudWatch performance counters CPU utilization, network in and network Out. If the CPU usage of the EC2 instance is less than 2% and the total number of bytes transmitted and received on all elastic network interfaces is less than 1000 bytes then the EC2 instance is flagged as Idle.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p>For Amazon EC2 your billed for any time your instance remains in running state, even partial hours get taken into account. To reduce associated costs, you can consider stopping/terminating instance or scale down instance size.<\/p>","bgp.route.flap.detected":"BGP route flap detected - unstable route announcements","site24x7.fullstack.agent.process.monitoring.rules.traditional":"For <b>traditional agent-based monitoring<\/b>, application processes that are already running when a Process Monitoring Rule is created must be restarted to create an APM monitor. For <b>eBPF-based monitoring<\/b>, the APM monitor is added automatically.","cl.dhcp.scan.status.desc":"Scan Status","alibabacloud_waf_v3.wafrate5m-wafv3":"WAF Rate 5m v3","velocloud.edges.list":"Select the Edges to be monitored.","cl.nw.storage.netapp.clusterpeer.icmp.ping":"Icmp Ping","thirdparty.lama.credential.tooltip":"Specify the company credentials required to login to your LAMA portal.","rum.source.upload":"Upload","thirdparty.azure.workspace.id":"Azure Log Workspace ID","alibabacloud_apsaradb_memcache.usedconnection":"Used Connection","js.statuspage.commenttime.pattern.error":"Invalid comment time pattern","predefined.report.19.name":"APM Downtime Summary","sdn.arista.probe.probe.http.response.millis.max":"Max Probe HTTP Response Time","global.server.myprofile":"My Profile","aws.rdspi.db.redo.edit":"DB Redo Edit","azure.supportshttps.trafficonly":"Supports HTTPS Traffic Only","al.db.top.ua":"User Agent Stats","reports.average.iis.exc":"Average Number of Exception Count","threshold.availability.vpc":"Performance Thresholds for VPC","transaction.details.viewdemo":"View Demo","cl.api.gateway.discover.message":"Your API Gateway Stages are being discovered.","az.title.vmscaleset.osdiskwriteoperationssec":"OS Disk Write Operations/Sec","step.one.active":"Step 1 Active","oci.drg.total.bytes":"Total Bytes","global.save":"Save","practice.aws.vpc.config.for.lambda.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p> Determines if your lambda functions have VPC configuration enabled for accessing the AWS resource privately.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p> By default, Lambda runs your functions in a secure VPC with access to AWS services and the internet. However, you can also configure your Lambda function to access resources with a custom VPC. A custom VPC defines a private network of resources, such as databases, cache instances, or internal services that allows you to connect to your Lambda function from within a VPC without internet access.<\/p><p> This method is used to block unauthorized outbound traffic to the internet. Several AWS services offer VPC endpoints. You can use VPC endpoints to connect to AWS services from within a VPC without internet access.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p> Add the VPC configuration to Lambda functions to access the AWS resources privately without internet access.<\/p>","azure.metric.RunningNodeCount.desc":"Number of running nodes","oci.ca.points":"<ul><li>Monitor certificate issuance and lifecycle events for better visibility.<\/li><li>Track Certificate Authority health and status.<\/li><li>Identify failed issuance or renewal operations.<\/li><li>Ensure secure and compliant certificate management.<\/li><li>Set threshold based alerts to detect abnormal behavior.<