,"oci.route.response.cache.action":"Response Cache Action","practice.aws.route53.dandling.dns.records.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p> Checks and identifies the Dangling DNS records in Route 53 cluster in order to maintain the security.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p> Check whether Dangling DNS entry , pointing to domain or subdomain, are deleted, in order to maintain security and prevent malicious access. If you leave a domain pointing at an IP address that you do not control, then there is a risk that someone may come along and claim traffic destined for your domain.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p> Remove all Dangling DNS entry in your domain.<\/p>","nutanix.add.container.li3":"Adding a Nutanix Storage Container is simple. Just add a Nutanix Cluster (under which your Storage Container is running) for monitoring, and enable autodiscovery for monitoring Nutanix Storage Containers.","oci.opensearch.general.information":"General information","nutanix.add.container.li1":"Obtain metric-level data of all storage containers that may affect the performance of your Nutanix environment.","glue.job.user":"Run Parameters","kube.vm.net.drops":"Network Drops","help.assistant.sns.content.1":"Visualize, monitor and alert on all the performance and usage metrics for your active SNS topics to understand the behavior of the pub/sub messaging and notification service powering your distributed application.","help.assistant.sns.content.2":"<ul><li>Number of messages published<\/li><li>Message size<\/li><li>Number of notification delivered/failed<\/li><li>SMS success rate.<\/li><\/ul>","help.assistant.sns.content.3":"<a href=\"{{help}}/aws/sns-integration.html\" target =\"_blank\"> Learn more<\/a>","nutanix.host.io.bandwidth.history":"Data transferred per second in MB/second from Hypervisor History","azure.metric.kube_node_status_allocatable_cpu_cores.disp":"Total number of available cpu cores in a managed cluster","cl.nw.ucs.san_port_channel.config.state":"SAN P