,"eks.memory.reserved.node":"Memory reserved for nodes","kube.services.name":"Service Name","msexchange.hub.access.fail":"Hub Transport Access Failure","virtual.interface.down":"{{n0}} : Virtual Interface is Down.","of365.verified.domains.count":"Verified Domains Count","saas.application.heroko.url":"Heroko URL","oci.storage.bucket.locked.until":"Locked Until","vpc.settings.autocreate.monitor.group.info":"Creates a monitor group for the Virtual Private Cloud.","aws.guard.duty.form.edit.monitor":"Edit GuardDuty Monitor","plugin.app.websphere.jdbc.createcount":"Create Count","country.oman":"Oman","oracle.db.metric.pgamaxmem.desc":"PGA Max Memory","practice.gcp.dns.key.signing.algorithm.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks whether deprecated algorithms are used for key signing in Cloud DNS managed zones.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p>The key signing algorithm is crucial for DNSSEC security. Using deprecated algorithms like RSASHA1 could compromise the security of your DNS infrastructure as they are considered less secure against modern cryptographic attacks.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p>Update your key signing algorithm to use more secure algorithms such as RSASHA256 or RSASHA512 instead of deprecated ones like RSASHA1.<\/p>","alibabacloud_apsaradb_hbase.blockcacheevictedcount":"Block Cache Evicted Count","aws.es.write.throughput.micro.bursting":"Write Throughput (Micro-bursting)","oracle.db.metric.snapshotparentconid.desc":"Snapshot Parent Connection ID","mssql.resp.lckwaits":"Lock Waits","global.configuration.error.devices":"Configuration Error Devices","rdspi.db.sql.tokenized.stats.local.blks.read.per.sec":"Local Blocks Read Per Second","applog.logtype.discovery.discoveredmon":"The following are the servers where we have discovered the above log types.","azure.indexersCount.report":"Indexers","vpc.az.monitor.edit":"Edit VPC Availability Zone Monitor Details","aws.glue.crawler.multiple.title":"Glue Crawlers","global.do.not.monitor":"Do Not Monitor","alibabacloud_ecs.intranetout":"Intranet Out","dashboard.perf.mulit.monitor.info":"Combine the data from these monitors into a single widget.","subscriptions.netflow.interfaces":"NetFlow Interfaces","aws.agentcore.policy.errors":"Policy Errors","footer.server.time":"Server Time","mssql.slowquery.minexectime":"Min Execution Time (ms)","practice.aws.disable.kms.keys.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks whether there have been any AWS CloudTrail events related to cryptographic operations performed using a KMS key over the last 90 days.<\/p><p><b>Description :<\/b><\/p><p>You are charged for KMS keys created in AWS regardless of usage until they're deleted. KMS keys that have not been used over the past 90 days are found using CloudTrail events, which capture all API calls to KMS. Verify if a key is being used before deleting it since this is destructive and potentially dangerous and may lead to data loss.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation :<\/b><\/p><p>Consider disabling unused KMS keys.<\/p><br><b>Note:<\/b><ul><li>Once a key is deleted, the data that was encrypted using the key can no longer be decrypted.<\/li><li>Public keys of asymmetric KMS keys can be downloaded and used outside of AWS, but CloudTrail logs do not record them. Thus, the usage of such keys cannot be determined using CloudTrail.<\/li><li>For unused asymmetric KMS keys, the private key part of the KMS key could be unused, but the public key part may still be in use outside of AWS and thus cannot be tracked using CloudTrail. Verify whether the public key is still being used before deleting the KMS key.<\/li><\/ul>","nsx.add.manager.li1":"Obtain metric-level data of all components like Management Nodes, Firewall policies, IP pools and Transport zones that affect the performance of your NSX-T Infrastructure.","multiple.azure.resource.files":"Azure File Shares","cl.core.perfValue":"Value (units)","client.marketing.dms.instance.bullet3":"The read-level actions necessary to discover DMS Repl