uns","mssql.db.lfs":"Log File Size","ec2.elasticinference.accelerator.memory.avg":"Average Accelerator Memory Usage","add.contact.enable":"Enable","thirdparty.slack.integ.level":"Choose the desired integration level to either push specific alerts from a monitor or all alerts from your Site24x7 account to the relevant Slack channel.<br><br>Select <b>Monitors<\/b> and choose the desired monitor to send out alerts and RCA links from the selected monitor alone to your Slack channel.<br><br>Select <b>All Monitors<\/b> to send out all Site24x7 alerts and RCA links to your desired Slack channel.<br><br>Select <b>Tags<\/b> and choose the desired tag to send Site24x7 alerts and RCA links to your desired Slack channel.","mssql.resp.wsmem":"Granted Workspace Memory","edit.az_signalr.monitor":"Edit Azure SingalR Monitor","site24x7.fullstack.agent.gotoapm.installation.complete":"Once the installation is complete, go to","azure.resource.loganalytics":"Azure Log Analytics Workspace","poller.logs.zipping":"Preparing Log Archive...","gcporg.discovery.submit.text":"Discover Organization","tpt.jira.integ.level":"Choose the desired integration level to create issues either for alarms from a specific set of monitors or from all your Site24x7 monitors.<br><br>Select <b>Monitors<\/b> and choose the desired monitors to create issues for alarms raised from those monitors.<br><br>Select <b>All Monitors<\/b>, to create issues for alarms from all Site24x7 monitors.<br><br>Select <b>Tags<\/b> and choose the desired tags to create issues for alarms raised from monitors associated or from monitors within monitor groups associated with those tags.","user.site24x7.options.note":"Note: Monitor Access, Voice Call and Alert Settings are applicable only to Site24x7","gcp.container.cpu.cores":"Container CPU Cores","ds.esxi.info":"ESXi Information","cl.nw.ucs.fabric.extender.serverPortsoperStateudldaggrdown":"Server Ports Oper State UDLD Aggr Down","tencentcloud_mysql.monitor.edit":"Edit Tencent Cloud MySQL Monitor","practice.instance.not.attached.to.iam.profile.role.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks the configuration of your monitored EC2 instances and identifies resources with no IAM role.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p>In a microservices architecture, the application running on EC2 instances needs to access resources running on other AWS services (S3 bucket, Lambda, DynamoDB, etc.) To enable, you can either create and distribute AWS credentials to the instances (and take up the overhead of rotating or updating them in the future) or delegate permission to make API requests using IAM roles.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p>Create an IAM role for your EC2 instances to delegate permissions or to perform actions on your behalf.<\/p>","aws.workspace.security.group":"Security Group","cl.nw.new.discovery.input.ncm.template":"Select NCM Device Template","aws.select.multiple.account":"Multiple Accounts","app.ibm_i.system_pools.db.faults.exceeds":"DB Faults Exceeds","alibabacloud_apsaradb_lindorm.lindorm_multi_thrift_call_num_ops":"Multi Thrift Call Number of Operations","aws.ssm.platform.name":"Platform Name","azure.metric.queuedqueries.desc":"Queued queries","mysqldb.performancemetrics.list":"MySQL Performance Metrics","mssql.db.lgs":"Log Growths and Shrinks","bulk.modify.user.groups":"Modify User Alert Groups","cl.core.import.task.aborted":"Your import task has been aborted. Please wait while we fetch the task status.","edit.az_containergroup.monitor":"Edit Azure Container Instance Monitor","sdn.common.max.temperature":"Max Temperature","glue.job.run.detail":"Job Run Details","lambda.logs.empty.message":"Log Stream for this Lambda Function contains no message.","azure.settings.guidance.usedefault.info":"The Guidance Report examines configuration and resource usage for AZURE services like Azure Virtual Machines, Azure App Service, and Azure Disk, using our 24 best practice checks and identifies resources that don't comply.","js.invalidemail":