ntgrid.publishsuccesslatencyinms":"Publish Success Latency In Ms","oci.autodb.storage.autoscale.increase":"Additional Storage Allocated","client.marketing.guard.duty.service.extra":"If you have disabled discovery and want Site24x7 to monitor your GuardDuty, then click on the Edit Integrated AWS Account button shown below, scroll down to the Discovery Options section, select the check box next to the GuardDuty listing and click on Save.","cl.ncm.actions.save.restart.info2":"Do you want to only save the configuration or save the configuration and restart the network module?","azure.metric.vmcachedbandwidthconsumedpercentage.desc":"VM Cached Bandwidth Consumed Percentage","azure.expressroute.globalReachEnabled":"Global Reach Enabled","practice.aws.efs.access.point.enforce.user.identity.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks if user identity is configured for monitored EFS (Elastic File System).<\/p><p><b>Description :<\/b><\/p><p>EFS clients like Amazon EC2 instances, containers launched by Amazon ECS, Amazon EKS services, and on-premise datacenters can be attached to EFS file systems. If POSIX (Portable Operating System Interface) user identity is configured for EFS access point then, all file system requests made through the access point from EFS clients are forced to use this identity thereby limiting the privileges of the EFS client. The user ID and group ID configured in POSIX user identity determines the privileges given to EFS client.<p>The user identity enforcement also does the following:<\/p><ui><li>The owner and group for new files and directories are set to the user ID and group ID of the access point.<\/li><li>EFS considers the user ID, group ID, and secondary group IDs of the access point when evaluating file system permissions. EFS ignores the NFS client's IDs.<\/li><\/ui><\/p><p><b>Recommendation :<\/b><\/p><p>Evaluate your choice of not configuring the user identity for access point.<br>(Note: POSIX user identity cannot be configured after creating an access point. You will have to create a new access point with the POSIX identity configured).<\/p>","global.Not.Applicable":"Not Applicable","report.mail.alibabacloud_apsaradb_selectdb.desc":"Report Mail Description","aws.valkey.cluster.shard.capacity.type":"Elasticache Valkey Cluster Shard Capacity","ecs.task.sets":"Task Sets","aws.nat.gateway.status.msg":"Status Message","alibabacloud_sae.instance_load":"Instance Load","aws.appsync.connect.success":"Connect Success","alibabacloud_fc.idleTimeout":"Idle Timeout","alibabacloud_apsaradb_hbase.slowgetcount":"Slow Get Count","cl.core.blk.act.task.progress.error":"The bulk action <b>{{n0}}<\/b> task is in progress with a few errors.","azure.metric.senderconnection.success.disp":"SenderConnections-Success","threshold.memory.util":"Memory Utilization threshold","apminsight.exception.source.splitup.graphheader":"Exception by Source","alibabacloud_disk.diskwriteiops":"Disk Write IOPS","oci.cache.help.doc.link":"<a href=\"{{help}}/oci/cache-monitoring.html\" target=\"_blank\"> Learn more<\/a>","vpc.avg.packets.dropped":"Avg Packets Dropped","login.user.password":"Password","alibabacloud_apsaradb_lindorm.searchupdatep99rt":"Search Update P99 RT","fabric.pod.id":"Pod ID","gateway.stage.cache.cluster.status":"Cache Cluster Status","subproduct.statuspage.announcement.content.statuspage.page":"Start using StatusIQ. You can still access your old pages till October 30.&nbsp;<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" ng-click=\"togglePage()\">Access Now<\/a>","alibabacloud_ecs.sysom_memmoninfo_used":"Memory Monitor Info Used","global.akamai_cloud_database.monitortype":"Akamai - Managed Database","alibabacloud_alb.LoadBalancerStatus":"Load Balancer Status","oci.dedicated.vm.supported.shapes":"Supported Instance Shapes","server.chart.title.disk.inode.individual":"Individual Disk Inodes Utilization","plugin.tab.custom.script":"Custom Monitoring With Zia","ebs.notification.endpoint":"Notification Endpoint","llm.chart.token.usage.for