 your secrets reduces the amount of time an unauthorized person can use a compromised secret.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation :<\/b><\/p><p>Consider enabling automatic rotation of Secrets Manager secrets.<\/p>","aws.asg.volume.disk.id":"Volume disk ID","metric.chart.name":"Metric : {{n0}}","gcp.metric.tempfileswrittencount.desc":"Temporary Files Used for Writing Data","add.gcp.monitor":"Add GCP Monitor","datalake.add.dependency.step2":"2. Add the dependency into your application based on your build framework","cl.server.metric.profile.memory":"Memory","cl.nw.storage.netapp.spare.disks":"Spare Disks","practice.aws.efs.enforce.root.directory.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks if EFS (Elastic File System) access point has root directory configured.<\/p><p><b>Description :<\/b><\/p><p>EFS clients like EC2 instances, containers launched by Amazon ECS, EKS services, and on-premise datacenters can be attached to EFS file systems. If root directory for EFS access point is configured then, EFS clients attached to the EFS file system access point can only have access to data in specified directory and its sub-directories. If not configured then, EFS client will have access to the root directory and its sub-directories.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation :<\/b><\/p><p>Evaluate your choice of not configuring the default root directory for access point.<br>(Note: Root directory cannot be configured after creating an access point. You will have to create a new access point with the default root directory configured).<\/p>","shrpt.oss.idlethreads":"Idle Threads","cl.server.upgrade.subagent.status":"Sub-Agent Status","plugin.app.jboss.webapp.sessions":"Web Application Sessions","mssql.avg.dlock":"Avg Dead Lock","of365.shp.inactive.drivedeploy.report":"Inactive Drive Deployment Report","cl.wlc.client.signal.strength.status.alert":"Alert if one or more client has low signal strength.","global.actions.reason":"Outcome Message","edit.alibabacloud_apsaramq_kafka.monitor":"Edit Kafka Monitor","ad.dns.server.down":"DNS Server Service is dowm","oci.certificate.name":"Name","iis.app.max.req.disconnect":"Max Disconnected Request","skype.chart.sip.instant.msg":"SIP Instant Messaging","unique.cloud.router.dynamic.route1":"Unique Cloud Router Dynamic Route Prefixes from Own Region per Region per VPC Network","practice.oci.application.tracing.disabled.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks whether distributed tracing is enabled for OCI Applications.<\/p><p><b>Description :<\/b><\/p><p>Distributed tracing provides end-to-end visibility into request flows across Application components, enabling latency analysis and root cause investigation.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation :<\/b><\/p><p>Enable distributed tracing for all OCI Applications.<\/p>","server.threshold.disk.status":"Notify when Disk Partition is Removed","alibabacloud_oss.mirror_request_count_by_status":"Mirror Request Count By Status","amazon.s3.list.request":"List Requests","r53.hostedzone.response.count":"Response Count","huaweicloud_evs.group.queue":"Queue Metrics","sdn.arubaedgeconnect.tunnel":"EdgeConnect Tunnel","stepfunction.definition":"Definition","podman.container.cpu.throttleperiod":"Container Throttle Period","oracle.rac.maxpgaalloc.desc":"Max PGA Allocation","cl.ncm.authorized":"Authorized","gcp.metric.dpc.hdfsstoragecapacity.desc":"HDFS Storage Capacity","alibabacloud_ecs.sysom_packetstatus_drop":"Packet Status Drop","velocloud.jitter.rx.max.max":"Jitter Rx Max Maximum","oci.permission.file.system.replication":"OCI File System Replication","kube.kproxy.pen.enpchg":"Pending Endpoint Changes","practice.oci.adb.adb.public.access.enabled.desc":"Autonomous database should not allow public access","ecmemcached.swap.usage":"Swap Usage(EC Memcached Cluster)","azure.metric.CapturedBytes.disp":"Captured Bytes.","global.unit.count.sec":"count/sec","azure.metric.plusstreamupstreampeerssslverifyfailureshostnamemismatch.desc":"Stream verify failure hostname mismatch","ba.funnel.kpi.request.attribut