acket.loss.rx.max":"Maximum Packet Loss Rx","azure.metric.RecordSetCapacityUtilization.desc":"Percent of Record Set capacity utilized by a DNS zone","aws.bedrock.invoke.agent.model.invocation.server.errors":"Agent Model Invocation Server Errors","azure.metric.ProtectedItemCount.disp":"Backup Items Count","alibabacloud_apsaradb_selectdb.instanceroutineloadjobnumbycancelled":"Instance Routine Load Job Number by Cancelled","apminsight.jira.ticket.creation.success":"Jira ticket created successfully","delegate.announce.req.reg":"Public Delegated Prefix Announce Requests per Minute per Project per Region","child.threshold.profile.edit":"Edit Child Entity Threshold Profile","alibabacloud_clb.newconnection":"New Connection","velocloud.packets.received.reason":"Packets Received {{n1}} (Packets) for {{n0}}","cl.nw.storage.netapp.aggregate.user.writes":"User Writes","bgp.hijack.moas.conflict":"<b>Multiple Origin AS (MOAS) Conflict<\/b><br> <i>Description:<\/i><br> Multiple Autonomous Systems are simultaneously announcing the same IP prefix, which may indicate a route hijack, misconfiguration, or legitimate multi-homing scenario that requires verification to ensure traffic is not being diverted to unauthorized networks.<br> <i>Detection:<\/i><br> Multiple Origin AS conflict detected for this prefix. Currently being announced by ASN {{n0}}, but the expected legitimate origin is ASN {{n1}}. While legitimate multi-homing scenarios exist, MOAS conflicts frequently indicate hijacking or misconfigurations. Verify with network operators whether this is authorized multi-homing or requires immediate remediation.","plugin.select.title":"50+ Out-of-the-Box Plugin Integrations","ds.monitoring":"Datastore Monitoring","anomaly.info.label":"Info","ecs.cpu.reservation":"CPU Reservation","gcp.sa.impersonation.validation.error2":"Please provide a valid service account email address.","oci.listener.name":"Listener Name","alibabacloud_analyticsdb_mysql.wlmsqaqueriespercentage":"WLM SQA Queries Percentage","subproduct.statuspage.migrate.announcement.line8.point4":"Status Pages feature in Site24x7 is <b>EOL-ed<\/b> and will not have any further development or support.","gcp.sa.impersonation.validation.error3":"Service account email is required and cannot be left blank.","gcp.sa.impersonation.validation.error4":"Service account email exceeds the allowed character limit.","subproduct.statuspage.migrate.announcement.line8.point2":"If you're a Site24x7 paid user you will be provided with three Basic status pages with all features supported in Site24x7 by default, and you need not pay anything for the existing features.<br>If you would like to use any advanced features of StatusIQ, you can buy Green Status Page add-on to enjoy the features.","subproduct.statuspage.migrate.announcement.line8.point3":"Understand the changes between both versions of status pages using our help guide. <a href=\"{{n0}}/statuspage/admin/statusiq-subscription.html#plans-features\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Help Resources.<\/a>","practice.kube.child.cpurequests.info.desc":"<h><b>Description : <\/b><\/h><p>Clusters cannot spread loads across nodes evenly when workloads do not specify container CPU requests. Configuring CPU requests to all workloads will enable the cluster to spread loads evenly.<\/br><\/p>","poller.group.monitor":"On-Premise Poller Group","rdspi.db.io.local.blks.read":"Local Blocks Read","subproduct.statuspage.migrate.announcement.line8.point1":"StatusIQ will be an enhanced version of Status Pages and  will be offering more features.","aws.ddb.title":"DocumentDB","of365.shp.allocated.drivesize.report":"Allocated Drive Size Report","cl.nw.add.credential":"Add a new SNMP Credential","azure.metric.action.successpercent":"Action Success Percentage","nutanix.disk.das.sata.usage":"Disk DAS-SATA Usage","cl.nw.voip.source.monitor.info":"<p>Please choose an existing Cisco monitor from the list.<\/p><p>These network devices are associated with Cisco device templates. The dev