ead Latency for Datastore \"{{n0}}\"  {{n1}}ms","sftp.summary.report":"SFTP Summary","aws.drs.recovery.instances":"Recovery Instances","committed.nvidia.a100.gpus.per":"Committed Nvidia A100 GPUs per Project Region","oci.info.private.key":"Paste the PEM-encoded private key corresponding to the API signing key. This will be stored encrypted.","azure.metric.Errors.disp":"Runtime Errors","sdn.cambium.switch.tx.pkts.err":"Tx Packet Errors","aws.sqs.avg.numofmsgsreceived":"Average Number Of Messages Received","global.screenshot.at":"at","rum.webvitals.cls.experience":"CLS Experience","aws.route53.hostedzone.monitortype":"Route 53 Hosted Zone","practice.aws.emr.via.vpc.desc":"Checks if Amazon EMR clusters are provisioned using the EC2-VPC platform instead of EC2-Classic platform.","cl.core.nu.verification.txt":"Hey! You've been invited to receive SMS status alerts. Please register your response by clicking the relevant button.","practice.gcp.vpc.legacy.network.in.use.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks if the legacy network routing mode is being used in your VPC configuration.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p>Legacy network mode uses an older routing configuration that lacks the advanced features and security controls available in more current VPC implementations. Legacy networks are single global networks with automatically generated IPv4 prefixes for all regions.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p>Migrate from legacy networks to VPC networks with regional subnets to take advantage of improved routing capabilities, better security controls, and more flexible IP address management.<\/p>","azure.resource.vm.capacity.type":"Azure Virtual Machine Capacity Planning","dbinsight.io.query.widget.title":"Top 10 Queries by Average Logical IO","huaweicloud_dds.mongo036_iops":"IOPS","huaweicloud_sfs.group.capacity":"Capacity Metrics","saas.application.wrike.title.add":"Add Wrike Monitor","sdn.xiq.switch.add.title":"Add ExtremeCloud IQ Switch","oci.opensearch.se