eport","msp.customer.portal.pattern":"Use only alphanumeric characters in Portal Name.","aws.bedrock.invoke.agent.model.invocation.count":"Agent Model Invocation Count","cl.nw.false.threshold":"Thresholds","azure.routes.subnets":"Routes and Subnets","redshift.queries.running.unload":"Unload Queries Running","nutanix.cluster.controller.io.bandwidth":"Data Transferred from the Storage Controller (MB/sec)","amazon.cs.domain.endpoint":"Domain Enpoint","practice.elb.with.cross.zone.disabled.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks if cross-zone load balancing is enabled in your Elastic Load Balancer configuration.<\/p> <p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p>By default Cross-Zone load balancing is not enabled for your classic type Elastic Load Balancer. Generally, a load balancer equally distributes incoming traffic across configured Availability Zones. However, there could be a mismatch in the load if you are not running an equivalent number of EC2 instances in each zone.This could easily happen as instances could get manually deregistered or detached due to health check failures or removed for maintenance. If cross-zone load balancing is enabled, then Elastic Load Balancer equally distributes application traffic to all registered instances.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p>Enable cross-zone balancing for your classic type Elastic Load Balancer.<\/p>","aws.dc.gateway.state.change.error":"State Change Error","plugin.app.websphere.topic.noofpublishers":"Number Of Publishers","practice.aws.mq.public.access.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p> Check if AWS MQ brokers are not publicly accessible to exposing sensitive data and minimize security risks.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p> Publicly available Amazon MQ brokers can be accessed directly, outside of a Virtual Private Cloud (VPC), Publicly accessible means anyone in the world can access your brokers through their public endpoints and this can increase the opportunity for malicious activity such as cross-site scripting (XSS) and clickjacking attacks.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p> Disable public accessiblity in Amazon MQ by recreating them with allow within VPC.<\/p>","alibabacloud_rds_mysql.sqlcommandmetrics":"SQL & Command Execution Metrics","nvidia.t4.virtual.workstation.gpus":"Nvidia T4 Virtual Workstation GPUs","reports.hyperv.rootvirtualprocessor.instructions":"Avg Root Virtual Processor Instructions","skype.dbs.sproc.latency":"DBStore - Sproc Latency","global.dashboard.choose":"Choose a Dashboard","sdn.arubaedgeconnect.sdwan.apikey":"API Key","cl.nw.storage.netapp.nfs.state.num":"NFS State","alibabacloud_ecs.instancememorysize":"Instance Memory Size","alibabacloud_apsaradb_clickhouse.clickhouse_distributed_files_count":"Distributed Files Count","azure.metric.outgoingallpnssuccess.disp":"Successful notifications","amazon.settings.servicequota.info":"Toggle Yes to manage your quotas for supported AWS services from Site24x7. <a href=\"{{site24x7.globals.help_file_url}}/aws/service-quotas.html\" target =\"_blank\"> Learn more<\/a>","query.checks.details":"Query Checks","adduser.read":"Read","global.number.short":"No.","global.wcag.open.newtab":"Open Link in new tab","plugin.configuration.suspicious":"Invalid entries detected. Please provide a valid configuration value.","oci.keys.edit":"Edit OCI Keys Monitor","wanrtt.monitor.total.failed":"Failed","alibabacloudnatgateway.limitsdropsandfailures":"Limits, Drops and Failures","wpa.dropdown.top20.scipt":"Top 20 JS","oracle.pdb.metric.undomode.desc":"Undo Mode","alibabacloud_apsaradb_clickhouse.disk_usage":"Disk Usage","server.id":"Server Id","aws.nat.avg.gateway.connection.attempt":"Average Connection Attempt Count","global.hostname":"Hostname","vpc.resource.name":"Resource Name","of365.alert.event.inbound.exceeds":"Inbound Message Exceeds","rds.amazon.other":"Other Engines - Threshold Configuration","global.wincls.monitortype":"Microsoft Failover Cluster","edit.az.lb.rule":"Edit Azure LB Rule","fsx.vol.