,"cl.nf.announcement.title.2":"Top N devices and interfaces","cl.nw.unable.to.fetch.wms.poller":"Unable to fetch the response from poller","cl.nf.announcement.title.3":"Stay on top of your network health","aws.valkey.conf.endpoint":"Configuration endpoint","vcloud.pvdc.vm.count.exceeds":"PVDC VM Count exceeds threshold","practice.gcp.pub.sub.unlabeled.topics.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks Cloud Pub/Sub topics to identify those without user-defined labels.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p>Labels are key-value pairs that help organize and categorize your Pub/Sub resources. Using labels enables better resource management, cost tracking, and filtering capabilities across your Google Cloud environment.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p>Apply meaningful labels to your Pub/Sub topics to improve resource organization, simplify management, and enhance cost allocation.<\/p>","web.application.monitor.about.desc":"Web Transaction monitor helps test whether transactions in web applications work as expected. It works even over authenticated sessions and help tests database and other backend uptime too by allowing verification of expected output content.","aws.inspector.findings.high.exceeds.count":"High Severity Findings {{n1}} Count","emr.no.monitoring.point.1":"Site24x7 give ops teams greater insight into the resource usage and performance of their AWS infrastructure and PaaS services with improved data retention, custom dashboards, reports, policy-driven thresholds and integrated notification channels.","emr.no.monitoring.point.2":"Enable Site24x7 to monitor all EC2 instances and S3 Buckets  underpinning your Elastic MapReduce environment to understand causes for Cluster degradation better.","alibabacloud_eip.SecurityProtectionTypes":"Security Protection Types","sdn.arista.org.add":"Add Organization","httpconfig.polling.internet.protocol.help.text":"Monitoring is performed over the selected internet protocol. While IPv4 or IPv6 is used in locations where the respective protocol is supported, the IPv4 or IPv6 option will help in flexibly switching to the protocol that is supported in a particular location if one protocol fails. IPv4 and IPv6 will create two connections for each protocol. \n IPv4 and IPv6 options will make two different connections to the configured URL. This will consume two basic monitor licenses.","vmware.vdi.rds.desktop.pool":"RDS Desktop Pool","ad.nspi.write.percentage":"NSPI Writes(%)","es.avg.credit.balance":"Average Credit Balance","oci.vcn.subnet.add":"Add OCI VCN Subnet Monitor","global.action.stop.function.apps":"Stop Function Apps","client.s3.metric.bullet5":"Generate performance reports for each supported attribute","azure.metric.miscerr.desc":"Other Errors (Deprecated)","iis.app.res.bytesent":"Total Bytes Sent(KB)","plugin.app.glassfish.widget.http.response.counts":"HTTP Response Counts","preemptible.nvidia.p4.vws.gpus":"Pre-emptible Nvidia P4 Vws GPUs per Project Region","practice.gcp.gke.integrity.desc":"In the Security section, check the Integrity monitoring feature status.","component.error.warning":"10-15% (Warning)","alert.p2s.connectioncount.tip":"Raw point-to-site connection count. The supported concurrent-connection ceiling is scale-unit-dependent and non-linear (500 for scale units 1-3, 1000 for 4-6, 5000 for 7-10, 10000 for 11-20, then 500 per scale unit beyond 20). No automatic default alert is set on this raw count; see P2S Connection Utilization for an alertable percentage of that scale-unit-derived ceiling.","azure.virtual.network.configuration":"Virtual Network Configuration","cl.thirdparty.product.eula.agreement":"By integrating with {{prod}}, you agree to the <a href=\"{{link}}\" target=\"_blank\">EULA<\/a> of {{prod}}.","tencentcloud_redis.Expired":"Expired Keys","server.add.service.mode.info":"Monitor services based on their start up mode.\nNote : If a startup type is not selected, all startup types will be monitored by default.","huaweicloud_vpn.unit":"Metrics","hyperv.form.memory.maximum":"Memory Maximum","global.add.domain.expiry":"Add a Domain Expiry monitor","oracle.db.metric.sharedpoolsize.desc":"Shared Pool Size","cl.nw.storage.devicemodel.label":"Device Model","practice.amazon.cloudfront.insecure.ssl.protocols.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p> Ensures that AWS CloudFront distributions origin(s) do not use insecure SSL protocols.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p> Using insecure and deprecated SSL protocols for your Cloudfront distributions could make the connection between the Cloudfront CDN and the origin server vulnerable to exploits such as POODLE (Padding Oracle on Downgraded Legacy Encryption). You're strongly recommended to use TLSv1.0 or later (ideally use only TLSv1.2 if you origins support it) and avoid using the SSLv3 protocol.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p> Remove the deprecated SSLv3 protocol from your Cloudfront distributions origin.<\/p>","cl.server.exclude.pattern":"Define the Exclude Pattern","jenkin.total.memory.initiated":"Total Memory Initiated","deep.discovery.new.bgp":"BGP Route","client.s3.metric.bullet3":"Gain insight into request rates and S3 workloads","client.s3.metric.bullet4":"Measure and monitor request latency, error count and error rate","vmware.vdi.vd.pcoip.imaging.bytes.sent":"Bytes Transmitted","client.s3.metric.bullet1":"Visualize bucket and object operations with preconfigured time series graphs","alibabacloud_mongodb.shardingttldeletedpsnode":"Sharding TTL Deleted Per Second Node","client.s3.metric.bullet2":"Get alerted on operational issues by setting up thresholds","cl.nw.discovery.report.no.devices.found":"No new devices found","huaweicloud_functiongraph.functionCost":"Function Cost","app.ibm_i.merged.chart.address.space.overview":"Address Space Overview","mysqlndbnode.metric.redologbuffertotal.desc":"Redo Log Buffer Total","iis.app.avg.sessqlconn":"Avg Session SQL Server connections","gcp.metric.bfd.receivedpacketscount.desc":"BFD Received packets count