cpu_user_usage":"User-mode CPU Time Percentage","iis.app.average.res.traffic":"Average Traffic","alert.azure.disk.not.attached":"Alert if disk is not attached","azure.metric.RowsWrittenPerSec.disp":"Processing: Rows written per sec","practice.azure.load.balancer.outbound.rules.with.default.port.allocation.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks if the load balancer outbound rules are using default port allocation.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p>Default port allocation for outbound rules might not be optimal for all scenarios and can cause a higher risk of source network address translation (SNAT) port exhaustion and scalability issues. Manual port allocation can help maximize the number of SNAT ports made available for each of the instances in your backend pool, which can help prevent your connections from being impacted due to port reallocation.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p>Review and customize the port allocation instead of the default port allocation setting for outbound rules to suit your application needs better.<\/p>","cl.nw.san.disk.used.bytes":"Disk Usage in bytes","add.contact.permissions.for.user":"Permissions","azure.metric.percentProcessorTime4.disp":"CPU (Shard 4)","azure.metric.HyperVToAzureProtectedItemsCount.disp":"HyperV to Azure Protected Items Count","standard.ndsv3.family.vcpus":"Standard NDSv3 Family vCPUs","jwt.web.tokens":"Web Tokens","amazon.ec.global.data.store.replication.lag":"Global Datastore Replication Lag","azure.dependency.view":"Dependency View","cl.nw.license.device.license.summary":"Device Level Usage Summary","az.title.workflow.runthrottledevents":"Run Throttled Events","alibabacloud_ecs.sysomschedmoniwait":"Scheduler Monitor Wait","practice.auto.scaling.template.auto.assign.public.ip.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks whether the launch templates associated with Amazon EC2 Auto Scaling group are configured to assign public IP to network interfaces upon launch.<\/p><p><b>Description :<\/b><\/p><p>Amazon EC2 instances in an Auto Scaling group launch configuration should not have an associated public IP address, except for in limited edge cases. Amazon EC2 instances should only be accessible from behind a load balancer, instead of being directly exposed to the internet.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation :<\/b><\/p><p>Consider disabling the Auto-assign public IP address option of Auto Scaling launch templates.<br>(<b>Note:<\/b> Modifying a launch template will create a new version of the template. Consider deleting older versions of the launch template if they're no longer required.).<\/p>","mongodbatlas.node.global.lock.current.queue.writers":"Global Lock Current Queue Writers","practice.aws.default.security.group.of.vpc.restricts.traffic.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p> Determines if the default security group of every VPC restricts traffic.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p> AWS Default security group does not restrict all inbound and outbound traffic. By default, VPC comes with a security group whose initial configuration denies all inbound traffic from internet and allow all outbound traffic. Configure all VPC default security groups to restrict all traffic so that the instance doesn't accidently send outbound traffic.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p> Ensure that AWS EC2 default security groups restrict all inbound traffic and enforce the users to create custom security groups instead of using default ones.<\/p>","multiple.azure.virtual.hub":"Azure Virtual Hubs","azure.metric.FailoverInProgressProtectedItemsCo.disp":"Failover in Progress Protected Items Count","tfa.push.denial":"Approval for this operation has been denied.","avg.oci.vcn.sl.usage":"Average Security List Usage","ec2.status.check.failures":"Status check failures","rdspi.os.diskio.nvme.4n1.avgreqsz":"Average Request Size (nvme 4n1)","practice.aws.waf.classic.webacls.contain.at.least.one.rule.or.rule.group.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks if Amazon WAF Classic WebACLs for Global and Regional types has at least one rule or rule group.<\/p><p><b>Description :<\/b><\/p><p>A WAF Global or Regional web ACL can contain a collection of rules and rule groups that inspect and control web requests. If a web ACL is empty, the web traffic can pass without being detected or acted upon by WAF depending on the default action.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation :<\/b><\/p><p>Consider configuring WebACLs to have at least one rule or rule group.<\/p>","oci.private.key.file.error":"Invalid file type. Only .pem files are accepted.","huaweicloud_gaussdbv5.monitor.type":"Huawei Cloud GaussDB openGauss","azure.unix.permissions":"Unix Permissions","gcp.quota.network.usage":"GCP Network Quota Usage","sdn.xiq.orchestrator.url.info":"URL of the ExtremeCloud IQ orchestrator","rbm.help.resources":"Help Resources","dscluster.read.latency":"Read Latency","oracle.db.metric.parsefailurecountpersec.desc":"Parse Failure Count per Second","server.disk.idle.per.mp":"Disk Idle percentage","azure.metric.usedips.desc":"Current ip usage","global.unit.mb":"MB","practice.api.gateway.enable.ssl.client.certificate.desc":"Checks if your Amazon API Gateway APIs are using SSL certificates to verify that HTTP requests made to your backend system are from API Gateway service.","aws.memorydb.search.based.set.cmds":"Search Based Set Commands","dns.flag.field":"Flag","al.lprof.aws.add.tooltip":"Add a new AWS account","global.view.comments":"View Details","aws.agentcore.memory.event.creation.count":"Events Created","server.newwindows.mssqlapp":"SQL","azure.metric.workflowactionscompleted.desc":"WorkflowActionCompletedCount","server.pkts.unit":"Packets","alibabacloudanalyticsdbpostgres.healthandspecializedmetrics":"Health and Specialized Metrics","sdn.catoNetworks.account.logical.id":"Logical ID","alibabacloud_apsaradb_selectdb.EngineMinorVersion":"Engine Minor Version","global.server.topprocmem":"Top Process by Memory","aws.valkey.nw.baseline.max.usage.out.percentage":"Network Baselin