WAF integration enables you to block any malicious requests made to your Cloudfront Content Delivery Network based on the criteria defined in the WAF Web Access Control List (ACL) associated with the CDN distribution. It helps protect against application-layer attacks that can compromise the security of your web applications or place unnecessary load on them.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p> Create the required WAF Access Control List and associate it with the appropriate web distribution to integrate CloudFront with AWS WAF.<\/p>","practice.azure.load.balancer.outbound.rules.with.default.port.allocation":"Azure Load Balancer - Outbound rule default port allocation","winbackup.disk.usedspace.exceeds":"Disk Used Space exceeds","saas.application.auth.url.info":"Please provide your customized Auth0 URL here.","cl.nw.san.eseries.disk.other.time.total":"Disk Other Time Total","cl.nw.netflow.status":"NetFlow Status","avg.readops.text":"Average Read rate","aws.rdspi.db.io.edit":"DB IO Edit","oci.basedb.pdb.redo.size":"Redo Generated","al.fwd.region.placeholder":"Select Region","disable.alert.msg":"Disable Alert","aws.secret.manager.rotated":"Secret Rotated","of365.reports.average.shp.freesitesize":"Average Free Site Size","practice.gcp.vpc.enable.vpc.flow.logs.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks if VPC Flow Logs are enabled for VPC subnets.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p>VPC Flow Logs record information about the IP traffic going to and from network interfaces in your VPC. This data is essential for network monitoring, forensic analysis, and security investigations. Without flow logs, you lack visibility into network traffic patterns that could indicate security issues or performance problems.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p>Enable VPC Flow Logs for all subnets to capture detailed network traffic metadata. Configure appropriate log retention periods and integrate with security monitoring systems. Consider sampling settings to balance visi