"Page Writes","practice.aws.route53.dns.alias.root.domain.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p> Checks DNS alias record available for ROOT Domain in AWS Route 53.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p> By creating Alias records for Amazon Route 53, it lets you route traffic to selected AWS resources, such as CloudFront distributions and Amazon S3 .Unlike a CNAME record, you can create an alias record at the top node of a DNS namespace. For example, if you register the DNS name example.com, the zone apex is example.com. You can't create a CNAME record for example.com, but you can create an alias record for example.com that routes traffic to www.example.com.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p> Ensure that DNS alias record set for the root domain within your AWS Route 53 hosted zone.<\/p>","aws.avg.sm.aws.secret.manager.rotate.secret.call.count":"Avg Secret Manager Rotate Secret call count","al.share.email":"Email","alert.network.error.exceeds":"Error Packets of \"{{n0}}\"  {{n1}} packets","sdn.arubaedgeconnect.help.assistant.purpose.title":"Purpose","oracle.tablespace.deleted":"Oracle Tablespace has been removed","mysql.help.doc":"<a href=\"{{help}}/database-monitoring/mysql-monitor.html#add-monitor\" target=\"_blank\">Follow the prerequisites and provide the user credentials with the required privileges<\/a>","lambda.edge.errors.threshold":"Errors (Regional Edge caches)","datalake.monitor.no.alerts.configured":"No alerts configured.","admin-msp.customer-management.customers.tour.1.accordian.msp.cust.mgmt.right":"<div><h5>Get to know your customers<\/h5><div>Get a bird's eye view of all your customer accounts and know the overall status of your customer infrastructure. Ensure that your customer accounts are managed efficiently.<\/div><\/div>","alert.azure.cpucore.change":"Alert if CPU Core is Changed","sdn.mist.errorcode.ratelimit":"Juniper Mist rate limit exceeded (5000/hr)","server.partition.disk.read.short":"Reads (Bytes/sec)","aws.waf.Requests":"Requests 