ensitive data. To fulfill compliance requirements encrypt your WorkSpaces storage volumes.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p> To encrypt existing AWS WorkSpaces data you must re-create the necessary WorkSpaces instances with the volumes encryption feature enabled.<\/p>","realbrowser.monitortype":"Web Transaction (Browser)","ad.app.avg.repobj.remaining":"Avg Replication Objects Remaining","esx.memory.heap":"Heap Memory (MB)","postgresql.insight.locks.by.mode":"Locks by Mode","alibabacloud_apsaradb_lindorm.handler_queue_size":"Handler Queue Size","of365.customapp.help":"Refer our <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"/help/admin/adding-a-monitor/office-365.html#auth-site24x7-custom-app\">help documentation<\/a> for step-by-step instructions.","amazon.ec.cache.hit.rate.avg":"Average Cache Hit Rate","gcp.metric.current.actions.desc":"Current Actions","client.marketing.inspector.service.bullet3":"The read-level actions necessary to discover Inspector \"inspector2:List*\" are not present in the assigned policy JSON.","client.marketing.inspector.service.bullet1":"There are no Inspector configured in the AWS account.","azure.metric.averageresponsetime":"Average Response Time (deprecated)","problem.timerange.customanalysis":"Time range must be within 1 hour of the problem start time.","vmware.health.dashboard.top.esx.cpu":"Top 10 ESX/ESXi Hosts by CPU","downloads.site.iphone":"Site24x7 iPhone App","databricks.job.tasks.lifecycle.title":"Task Lifecycle States","aws.tg.packets.in.count":"Packets In (Count)","client.marketing.oci.filesystem.bullet1":"There are no File Systems configured in your OCI account.","client.marketing.oci.filesystem.bullet2":"You have opted out of monitoring by unselecting the checkbox next to the File Storage listing.","client.marketing.oci.filesystem.bullet3":"The read-level actions necessary to discover File Systems are not present in the assigned policy.","oci.postgres.db.write_throughput_primary_role.desc":"Write Kilobytes (Replica)","al.fwd.section.filtering.info":"Restrict which logs are forwarded by log type and query.","practice.sqs.dead.letter.queue.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks and identifies standard or FIFO queues with no designated dead letter queue.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p>A dead letter queue is an undelivered message queue to which messages get sent when they are not successfully processed by the consumer. Users can use this holding queue to isolate and troubleshoot problematic messages and determine why their processing failed.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p>Dead letter queues can't be configured for existing queues. Configure a new SQS source queue and create a second queue as a dead letter queue.<\/p>","aws.appstream.active.session.count.userpool":"Active Sessions (Userpool)","al.db.error.400.rate":"Error Rate 4xx by Code","huaweicloud_obs.capacity_total":"Total Storage Capacity","ecs.hard.limit":"Hard limit","nutanix.cluster.cache.num.hits.history":"Number of hits on the content cache History","rdspi.os.diskio.rdstemp.avgqueuelen":"RDS Temp Disk I/O Average Queue Length","poller.group.chart.title.moncount":"Monitors Associated with On-Premise Pollers","cl.nw.san.interface.edit.title":"Edit Interface","aci.controller.name":"Monitor Name","static.byoip.ip.addresses":"Static Byoip Ip Addresses","app.ibm_i.report.avg.security.level":"Avg Security Level","oci.apigw.http.bytes.sent":"Http Backend Bytes Sent","esx.hardware.memory.status":"Notify when a Memory Sensor is Down/Trouble/Unknown","global.listpage.restapi.graphql":"REST API Monitor - GraphQL","edit.az.eventgrid.systemtopics":"Edit Azure Event Grid System Topic","alibabacloud_oss.intranet_send_bandwidth_usage_rate":"Intranet Send Bandwidth Usage Rate","device.threshold.interface.rx.nonunicast.packets":"Non-Unicast Packets Received {{n1}} (Per Second) for {{n0}}","dynamodb.metric.prov.read.cap.min":"Provisioned Read Capacity Units Minimum","alert.digitalocean.algorithm.change":"Alert when Algorithm is Changed","add.azure.resource.data.explorer.cluster":"Add Azure Data Explorer Cluster","practice.igw.name":"Internet Gateway Name","oracle.insight.sessions_suspended":"Sessions Suspended","alibabacloud_apsaradb_hbase.memnonheapusedm":"Non-Heap Memory Used (MB)","aws.ha.subsection.application.integration":"Application Integration","azure.lb.probe":"Azure LB Health Probe","admin-bu.bu-management.business-units.tour.1.addiconsitem.client.user.alerts.right":"<div><h5>Add, Manage and Alert<\/h5><div>Add more users, assign unique access privileges to them and opt whom to be alerted during an outage as well as the mode of notification.<\/div><\/div>","alibabacloud_oss.sync_send":"Sync Send","help.assistant.oci.feature.title.subtitle.three":"Forecasting","proxmox.node.add.li3":"Adding a Proxmox Node is simple. Just add a Proxmox Cluster (under which your Node is associated) for monitoring, and enable autodiscovery for monitoring Proxmox Nodes.","global.deployfile.approve":"By clicking Upload & Deploy, I authorize Site24x7 to save the given file and push it to the selected servers.","global.glassfish.monitortype":"GlassFish","proxmox.node.add.li4":"Proxmox Node are currently licensed as host monitors.","msex.asset.max.rcv.size":"Max Receive Size","oci.mdb.channel.failure":"Inbound Channel Failure","apminsight.drop.threshold.info":"* Method calls less than {{drop_threshold}} ms are not shown","shrpt.oss.queuescommiting":"Committing Queues","kube.node.volume.inodes.mp":"Total Inodes (Linux)","r53.resolver.inbound.query.endpoint":"Endpoint - Inbound Query Volume","oci.mt.kerberos.realm":"Kerberos Realm","min.application.requests5XX":"Application Requests With 5XX Status (Min)","practice.gcp.lb.logging.enabled.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks if logging is enabled for Google Cloud load balancers.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p>Load balancer logs provide valuable information about request patterns, client IP addresses, response status codes, and latency metrics. Without logging, you lose visibility into traffic patterns, making it difficult to troubleshoot issues, detect security incidents, or optimize performance.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p>Enable logging for all load balancers to capture request and response data. Configure appropriate sample rates to balance visibility with cost if necessary. Integrate logs with monitoring and security tools to gain insights into traffic patterns and potential security issues.<\/p>","practice.oci.sgw.route.table.missing":"OCI Service Gateway - Route Table Missing","ncm.compliance.rule.advanced.criteria.option1":"should contain","predefined.report.101.description":"Swap usage and page fault metrics for servers","ncm.compliance.rule.advanced.criteria.option2":"should not contain","postgresql.insight.total.io.time":"Total IO Time","oci.postgres.node.restart":"Restart Postgres DB Node","cl.ncm.system.location":"System Location","cl.ncm.credential.profile.report":"Credential Details Report","mssql.max.fs":"Max Full Scan","gcporg.discover.projects":"Auto Add Project Monitors","vmware.vdi.vd.pcoip.network.rx.peak.bandwidth.kbps":"Peak Bandwidth for Incoming Packets (kbit/s)","global.max.mem.lim":"Maximum Memory Limit","ad.dra.replicated.objects":"DRA Replication Objects","global.slo.compliance":"SLO Compliance","server.msexchange.hub.trans.queue.msg.title":"Hub Transport queue messages","ssl.cert.subjectalternativename":"Subject Alternative Name(SAN)","server.resource.notify.down":"Alert when a resource check profile fails","practice.azure.vm.bootDiagnostics.info.desc":"<h><b>Description : <\/b><\/h><p><ul><li>Boot Diagnostics in Azure VMs is a feature that enables capturing and analyzing boot-time logs and screenshots, offering insights into the startup process and potential issues during VM boot.<\/li><li>It assists administrators in diagnosing and resolving boot-related issues efficiently.<\/li><\/ul><\/p>","proxmox.node.add.li1":"Analyze the resource utilization in your Promox nodes by monitoring various performance metrics.","plugin.app.glassfish.report.heading.filecache.misses":"Average Misses","cl.core.imp.task.success":"Monitors added successfully","elb.tg.initial":"Initial","alibabacloud_oss.InternetSendBandwidthUsageRate":"Internet Send Bandwidth Usage Rate","lambda.logs.empty.info":"Logs is empty","ec2.ebsactivity.graph.title":"EBS I/O Operation Activity (CloudWatch)","az.title.adp.activitysucceededruns":"Succeeded Activity runs","alibabacloud_polardb.clusterblktagutilization":"Cluster Block Tag Utilization","alibabacloud_oss.qos_max_intranet_recv_flow":"Qos Max Intranet Recv Flow","jsp.tools.json-path-evaluator.inputpath":"Input Path Expression","plugin.app.glassfish.metric.total2xx":"Total2Xx","oci.certificate.associations.filter.label":"Filter Certificate Associations","reports.server.time.units":"Server Time (ms)","zia.agent.execute":"Execute Agent","reports.unmanaged.maintenance.summary":"Monitor Suspended Summary","practice.aws.s3.bucket.cloudtrail.logs.publicly.accessible.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p> Determines if your S3 bucket CloudTrail logs are publicly accessible or not.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p> Amazon S3 buckets and objects are private by default, and only the individual who created the bucket can access them and the objects it contains. CloudTrail logs could include detailed events of API activity in your account. When you provide an insecure set of permissions for your CloudTrail logging of S3 buckets, you could provide malicious users access to your AWS account log data which can increase the risk of unauthorized access.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p> Ensure that the associated S3 bucket for CloudTrail logging are not publicly accessible and safeguard your AWS account log data.<\/p>","wincls.timer.service":"Timer Service","bulk.action.child.threshold.child.type.required":"Select a child entity type in the filter before continuing.","oci.app.error.rate":"Error Rate","global.OS.Requ