y Resource monitor to track and alert on API execution metrics for all individual resources and methods associated to any API stage. Prerequisites are","aws.bedrock.query.engine.workgroup.arn":"Query Engine Redshift Workgroup ID","practice.gcp.kube.enable.network.policy.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks whether Network Policy is enabled on your GKE clusters.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p>Network Policy allows you to control pod-to-pod communication within your cluster. Without Network Policy enabled, all pods can communicate with each other, which could lead to unauthorized access between application components.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p>Enable Network Policy on your GKE clusters to implement fine-grained control over pod-to-pod communication and improve your cluster's security posture.<\/p>","global.spokesperson.details.txt":"Read/Write permission allows the spokesperson to add public comments.","practice.gcp.sql.enable.pg.audit.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks if the pgAudit extension is enabled for PostgreSQL instances.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p>The pgAudit extension provides detailed session and object audit logging capabilities that are often required for regulatory compliance. It provides more comprehensive auditing than PostgreSQL's native logging functionality.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p>Enable the pgAudit extension in your CloudSQL PostgreSQL instance to meet compliance requirements and enhance security monitoring capabilities.<\/p>","share.account.access.help.info":"Toggle to Yes to share your account details with the Site24x7. This setting will remain active for 30 days, after which it will automatically revert to the setting configured on the My Accounts page.","global.ip.continent.wise":"Continent-wise listing of our monitoring locations along with their IP addresses.","az.title.containergroup.networkbytestransmittedpersecond":"Network Bytes Transmitted Per Second","reports.average.ad.iodbreads":"Average I/O Database Reads","cl.core.dash.primary.loc":"Primary Location","alibabacloud_apsaramq_kafka.VSwitchIds":"VSwitch Ids","global.trend.period":"Trend Period","statusboard.stat.typelist.host_monitors.weightage":"<p class=\"line-ht16\">You've consumed {{total}}/{{allowed}} host monitor licenses in your subscription. {{monCount}} {{monType}} monitors used {{used}} out of {{total}} active host monitor licenses. (Note: {{unit}} in {{monType}} consumes one basic monitor license.)<\/p>","global.freespace":"Freespace","azure.metric.Average_AvailableMBytes.disp":"Available MBytes","network.credential.sync.message":"Synchronize credentials from the MSP admin.\nNote: This can be triggered once every five minutes.","ad.db.threads":"Threads","help.assistant.bedrock.content.3":"Get an account-wide rollup of model, agent, and guardrail activity in a region, along with your estimated tokens-per-minute quota usage.","help.assistant.bedrock.content.2":"<a href=\"{{help}}/aws/bedrock-integration.html\"target =\"_blank\"> Learn more<\/a> about Amazon Bedrock Monitoring.","help.assistant.bedrock.content.5":"Know how your agents perform end to end - invocation counts, total response time, time to first token, orchestration model calls, and client, server, and throttling errors.","client.marketing.dms.task.extra":"If you have disabled discovery and want Site24x7 to monitor your DMS Replication Tasks, then click on the Edit Integrated AWS Account button shown below, scroll down to the Discovery Options section, select the check box next to the Database Migration Service listing and click on Save.","help.assistant.bedrock.content.4":"Track invocation counts, latency, success rate, throttles, and input and output token consumption for each foundation model you invoke.","client.marketing.glb.info":"Monitor the performance of your Gateway ELB nodes by analysing critical metrics like traffic, active connections and connection rate.","help.assistant.bedrock.content.7":"Keep track of the configuration and status of every knowledge base backing your retrieval augmented generation workflows.","huaweicloud_vpcep.tab.RST_Packets":"RST Packets","help.assistant.bedrock.content.6":"Measure how often your guardrails are invoked, how often they intervene on unsafe content, intervention rate, evaluation latency, and text units processed.","oci.apigw.backend.504.backend.http.responses":"Backend 504 Backend HTTP Responses","cl.nw.ucs.vsan.config_overlap":"VSAN Config Overlap","aws.tg.attach.route.table.alert":"Notify when route table is modified","help.assistant.bedrock.content.1":"Monitor the availability, performance, and token consumption of your generative AI workloads on Amazon Bedrock.","practice.api.gateway.api.stages.aws.x.ray.tracing.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks if monitored API Gateway resources have X-ray tracing enabled.<\/p><p><b>Description :<\/b><\/p><p>AWS X-Ray can be used to trace and analyze user requests as they travel through your Amazon API Gateway REST APIs to the underlying services. X-Ray gives you an end-to-end view of an entire request, so that you can analyze latencies in your APIs and their backend services. X-Ray tracing enables a more rapid response to performance changes in the underlying infrastructure.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation :<\/b><\/p><p>Consider enabling X-ray tracing for API Gateway.<\/p>","global.listpage.bulk.restapi.info":"Bulk import your API endpoints from your predefined Swagger (JSON), HAR or CSV files.","al.db.jen.class":"Top ClassName","details.menu.edit.desc":"Associate thresholds, users for alerts, change monitor settings.","oracle.db.listener.port.bind.status":"Port Binding Status","ses.delivery.topic":"Delivery Topic","amazon.elb.ELB3xx.report":"ELB 3XX Errors","cl.wlc.ap.max":"Max AP Count","ncm.configlets.info.remediation.template":"Select a configuration template that must be executed when there is a compliance rule violation.","sdn.celona.ap.default.max.transmit.power