o.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks whether the workspace restricts public network access.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p>Restricting public access to workspaces ensures that the workspace is not exposed to the public internet, reducing the risk of unauthorized access and potential security vulnerabilities.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p>Consider disabling public network access to the workspace.<\/p>","al.db.jen.top.job":"Top JobNames","client.marketing.restapi.info":"REST API Monitor evaluates the uptime, performance, and correctness of your API endpoint. Define specific expression assertion, validate and get notified if the response data from JSONPath, XPath, or Text data fails.","plugin.mysql.total.blocks":"Total Blocks","alibabacloud_clb.instancestatuscodeother":"Instance Status Code Other","aws.redshift.workgroup.address.type":"Address Type","cl.fullstackagent.bulk.action.version.info":"Agents will be upgraded to the this agent version.","postgresql.metric.walcompression.desc":"WAL compression","ec2.ebs.read.bytes.avg":"Average EBS Read Bytes","rum.metric.dlt":"Document Download Time","msp.apply.license.cap.basic":"Define an upper usage limit to restrict basic monitor usage in the customer account. Once you touch the usage limit, you can't add any more basic monitors, unless you increase the limit manually. Other customers can still utilize any unused monitors.","bgp.hijack.sub.prefix":"<b>Sub-Prefix Hijack (More-Specific Prefix)<\/b><br> <i>Description:<\/i><br> A sophisticated BGP hijack technique where an attacker announces a more specific (longer) prefix than the legitimate owner's announcement, exploiting BGP's longest-prefix-match routing rule to attract and intercept traffic intended for the original prefix.<br> <i>Detection:<\/i><br> Sub-prefix hijack detected - ASN {{n0}} is announcing a more specific prefix than the expected announcement from ASN {{n1}}. BGP routers prefer longer prefix matches, causing traffic to be diverted to this more specific route. This is a common and effective hijack technique requiring immediate investigation to determine if the more-specific announcement is legitimate or malicious.","bgp.threshold.total.prefixes":"Total Prefixes Threshold","plugin.app.websphere.queues.oldestmessageage":"Oldest Message Age Sec","threshold.processrunning.mp":"Number of Running Processes in Queue","aws.elastic.ip.associated.ip.count.avg":"Average Attached IP(s)","alibabacloud_ecs.sysom_pingtrace_ltxmergedkern":"Ping Trace LTX Merged Kernel","smtp.mail.delay.exceeds.threshold":"Notify when the email latency exceeds the threshold","oracle.db.metric.physicalwritespersec.desc":"Physical Writes per Second","tencentcloud.authtype.header.desc.1":"<div>1. Log in to the <a href=\"https://console.tencentcloud.com/cam\">Cloud Access Management<\/a> (CAM) console in Tencent.<\/div><div>2. Go to <b>Access Management <\/b> >  <b>Users<\/b> > <b>User List<\/b>.<\/div><div>3. Click the sub-user you want to use for monitoring.<\/div><div>4. Go to the <i>API Key<\/i> tab. If no key exists, click <b>Create Key<\/b>.<\/div><div>5. Click <b>Show<\/b> and copy the <i>Secret ID<\/i> and <i>Secret Key<\/i>.<\/div>","app.ibm_i.report.max.batchjobsending":"Max Batch Jobs Ending","docker.container.alertmsg.down":"Container \"{{n0}}\" is down.","global.server.port.info":"Check if a port is accessible on the server.","rds.snapshot.storage":"Snapshot Storage Used","cl.nw.storage.netapp.nfs.nfsv3.read.throughput":"Nfsv3 Read Throughput","cl.nw.ucs.virtual_circuit.vnic.tx.bytes":"Virtual Circuit vNIC TX Bytes","ping.host.field.help.text":"Specify the IP address or domain name of the host to ping.","aws.waf.rulegroup":"Rule group and Condition Details","s3.replication.rules":"Replication Rules","dashboard.display.size":"Display Size","static.global.external.ipv4.and":"Static Global External Ipv4 And Ipv6 Addresses","cl.nw.topn.interface.tx.utilization.title":"Top 10 Interfaces by Tx Utilization","oci.vcn.security