nt.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p> Elastic IPs (EIPs) allow users to mask instance failure or software failure by rapidly remapping the address to another instance in the same account. AWS enforces an hourly charge if an EIP address within your account isn't associated with a running EC2 instance or an Elastic Network Interface (ENI).<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p> Remove any unused EC2 EIP addresses in your AWS account and release them to avoid excessive charges to your monthly AWS bill.<\/p>","cl.recommendation.network.700005.title":"Troubleshoot connectivity or high traffic with SNMP Traps","device.reports.average.bufmiss":"Avg Buffer Miss","alibabacloud_apsaradb_lindorm.lindormmultiworkercount":"Multi Worker Count","oci.api.deployment.rate.key":"Rate Key","home.action.notallowed":"No Actions Allowed","client.no.aws.childmonitor.found.reasons.four":"You have disabled discovery by unchecking the said AWS service in the \"Services to be discovered field\" in Add/Edit Amazon Web Services form.","container.io.total":"I/O Total (MB)","app.ibm_i.metric.maximumjobsinsystem":"Maximum Jobs in System","alibabacloud_nas.alignedsize":"Aligned Size","practice.aws.emr.logging.enabled.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p> Checks whether Amazon EMR cluster log files are enabled to upload in S3.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p> By enabling the logging AWS for EMR , it will help us to maintain the historical data of EMR Cluster. By default, all log files automatically deleted from the cluster. These files are helpful in the analysis and debuging any issues related with EMR cluster.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p> Enable the setting, for log files to be stored in S3.<\/p>","neptune.http.5xx":"Http5xx","msp.bulk.inprog.profile.count":"In Progress Profiles Count","server.unreclaimable.memory":"Unreclaimable Memory","msexchange.db.io.read":"I/O DB reads avg latency","apminsight.graphs.msg.renderingcharttext":"Rendering Chart. Please Wait.","iampolic