e network level protection and additional security benefits for your GKE cluster.<\/li><li>Authorized networks grant access to a specific set of trusted IP addresses, such as those that originate from a secure network.<\/li><li>This can help protect access to your GKE cluster in the case of a vulnerability in the cluster's authentication or authorization mechanism.<\/li><\/ul><\/p>","es.avg.kms.key.inaccessible":"Average KMS Key Inaccessible","cl.nw.meraki.help.assist.purpose.label":"Purpose","aws.cs.stemming.key":"Keys","threshold.task.networkIn.exceeds":"{{n0}} : Task Definition No of Bytes Received {{n1}} MB.","reports.cdn.edge.server":"CDN edge server","app.ibm_i.report.max.usersuspendedbysystemrequest":"Max Users Suspended by System Request","nutanix.cluster.controller.read.io.bandwidth.report":"Read data transferred in MB/second from the Storage Controller Report","cl.server.errorlog.file.checks":"Error Log File Checks","alert.oracle.listener.service.tnst":"Oracle Listener service TNS status of \"{{n0}}\" {{n1}}.","practice.kinesis.stream.kms.encrypted.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks for Amazon Kinesis Data Streams where Server-Side Encryption (SSE) is enabled by AWS managed CMKs.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p>CMKs (Customer Master Keys) are the primary resource used to encrypt and decrypt data. There are three types: customer managed CMKs, AWS managed CMKs, and AWS owned CMKs. You can either encrypt data in your Amazon Kinesis Streams using AWS managed CMKs or create your own customer managed CMKs for more control and flexibility.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p>Use customer managed CMKs to encrypt data at rest within the Kinesis Data Stream service.<\/p>","oci.mt.general.information":"General Information","global.baseitem.rum":"RUM","alert.oracle.listener.service.tnsp":"Oracle Listener service TNS time of \"{{n0}}\" {{n1}} ms.","gcp.sync.org.settings":"Sync Settings from GCP Organization Monitor","kube.container.env":"Environm