s that allow or deny access to a specific port or IP range. An AWS NACL contains a numbered list of rules that are evaluated in order, starting with the lowest numbered rule (e.g. 100), to determine whether the traffic is allowed in or out of the associated VPC subnet(s). The order of the DENY rules within your Network ACLs is crucial as these are evaluated in order and any ineffective or deficient DENY rule can be applied regardless of any higher-numbered rule that may contradict it.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p> Reconfigure any ineffective or mis configured AWS NACL DENY rules in order to block the traffic to the necessary port at the subnet level.<\/p>","aws.appsync.publish.data.message.client.error":"Publish Data Message Client Error","sdn.mist.wan.edge.memory2.util":"HA Secondary Memory (%)","aws.region.ap-southeast-3":"Asia Pacific (Jakarta)","msexchange.rpc.request":"RPC Requests","amazon.errorcode.11006":"AWS - Authorization Failed - Insufficient Permission to access selected Resource(s)","aws.region.ap-southeast-5":"Asia Pacific (Malaysia)","amazon.errorcode.11005":"AWS Account is affected by a health event","aws.region.ap-southeast-4":"Asia Pacific (Melbourne)","gcp.quota.cloudfunction.usage":"GCP Cloud Function Quota Usage","amazon.errorcode.11004":"Connection Not Available","server.process.cpu.exceeds":"Process CPU Utilization Exceeds","global.notapplicable":"N.A","aws.region.ap-southeast-7":"Asia Pacific (Thailand)","amazon.errorcode.11003":"AWS - Service Not Available - Target Server Failed to Response","vitual.netadap.bytessentpersec.exceeds":"Virtual Network Adapter Bytes Sent Per Sec Exceeds","mssql.longtranstime.history":"Longest Transaction Time History","practice.azure.ml.workspace.cmk.encryption.desc":"Ensure that machine learning workspaces use customer-managed keys (CMKs) for encryption.","statsd.monitor.action.enable":"Enable StatsD","server.cpu.percent":"CPU (%)","apm.section.fullstack.child.linux.title":"Linux Server","amazon.err