dashboard.free.page.count.chart.name":"Free Page Count Report","ncm.compliance.info.policy.description":"Provide a description for the compliance policy.","rds.tempdb.avail.data.space":"Tempdb Available Data Space","rule.network.device.category":"Network Device Category","oci.postgres.db.used_storage.desc":"Used Storage","aws.ddb.global.cluster.resource.id":"Global Cluster Resource ID","client.events.cloudspend.az.popup.1":"CloudSpend Azure","client.events.cloudspend.az.popup.2":"CloudSpend Azure helps you control cloud costs, optimize resources, and achieve cloud cost visibility.<a href=\"{{help}}/cloudspend/azure/integrate.html\" target =\"_blank\"> Learn more.<\/a>","country.liechtenstein":"Liechtenstein","rum.waterfalls.analysis":"Waterfall Analysis","mssql.ls.history":"Log Shrinks History","mssql.lfs.report":"Log File Size Report","health.check.period.lastpolled":"The Health Check count is defined based on the selected time period. It displays the last polled data for the time period selected.","aws.agentcore.browser.list.errors":"Browser List Errors","standard.dsv2.promo.family.vcpus":"Standard DSv2 Promo Family vCPUs","network.help.credential.pt7":"<ul><li>Save the credential<\/li><\/ul>","client.marketing.agentcore.memory.service.bullet3":"The read-level actions necessary to discover AgentCore Memory resources  \"bedrock-agentcore:List*\" and the related \"bedrock-agentcore:Get*\" read actions are not present in the assigned policy JSON.","network.help.credential.pt6":"<ul><li><b>Display Name:<\/b> Enter the display name of the credential.<\/li><li><b>Description:<\/b> Enter a brief description about the credential.<\/li><li><b>User Name: <\/b> Enter the name of the user (principal) on behalf of whom the message is being exchanged.<\/li><li><b>Context Name: <\/b>An SNMP context name or \"context\" in short, is a collection of management information accessible by an SNMP entity. An item of management information may exist in more than one context. An SNMP entity potentially has access to many contexts. In other words, if a management information has been defined under a context by an SNMPv3 entity, then any management application can access that information by giving that context name. The \"context name\" is an octet string, which has at least one management information.<\/li><li><b>Authentication:<\/b> Select any of the authentication protocols either MD5 or SHA and enter the password. MD5 and SHA are processes which are used for generating authentication/privacy keys in SNMPv3 applications.<\/li><li><b>Encryption:<\/b> Select any of the encryption protocols either DES or EAS-128 and enter the password. Note: Only after configuring Authentication it is possible to configure Encryption.<\/li><li>SNMP Port: Enter the SNMP port number.<\/li><\/ul>","network.help.credential.pt5":"<b>SNMP v3:<\/b> SNMPv3 is a user based security model. It provides secure access to the devices by a combination authenticating and encrypting packets over the network. The security features provided in SNMPv3 are Message integrity, Authentication and Encryption. If you select SNMPv3 as the credential type, then configure the following parameters.","website.defacement.script.threshold.info":"Threshold value to determine script content breach. Any script content included in the web page when modified beyond this \u201CScript Defacement\u201D threshold value will render the web page in trouble and trigger an alert.","network.help.credential.pt4":"<b>SNMPv1 / SNMPv2:<\/b> SNMPv1 and SNMPv2 are community based security models. Enter the Display name and description. Configure the correct Read and Write (optional) community, SNMP Port, SNMP Timeout (in seconds) and SNMP Retries.<br><br>","network.help.credential.pt3":"<ul><li>Go to Network > Settings.<\/li><li>Click Add Credential in this screen.<\/li><li>Select the relevant protocol:<\/li><\/ul>","sdn.mist.ap.topn.mem.used.kb":"Juniper Mist APs by Memory Used (KB)","network.help.credential.pt2":"Steps to Add a new Credential","cl.nw.storage.netapp.interface.Inbound.bps":"Inbound Bps","network.help.credential.pt1":"Site24x7 accesses the remote devices using the SNMP protocol. The SNMP community may differ for different device types. Pre-configuring a set of credentials in Site24x7 helps applying them to multiple devices at a time, saving a lot of manual effort.","client.select.resource.names":"No Resources associated with this type","search.help.commands.adminactions":"Search operations available under the Admin tab","monitor.group.get.started":"Get started by creating your group","gcp.metric.scheduledsize.desc":"Scheduled size","rdspi.db.temp.temp.files":"Temporary Files","al.upgrade.suggestion.label":"AppLogs upload size per month (GB)","winbackup.monitor.add":"Add winbackup monitor","global.alibabacloud_gwlb.monitortype":"Alibaba - Gateway Load Balancer","plugin.app.glassfish.report.heading.initheapsize.count":"Average Init Heap Size","global.primary.location":"Primary Location","aws.dlm.ebs.snapshot.snapshots.delete.completed":"Snapshots Delete Completed","alibabacloud_fc.functionmaxmemoryusage":"Function Max Memory Usage","azure.resource.triggeredjob.promptlabel":"Triggered WebJob","amazon.rdspi.os.disks.instanceid.text":"OS Disks Instance ID","sdn.arubacentral.link.isp":"ISP / Provider","sdn.common.probe.http.response.time":"Probe HTTP Response Time","web.monitors.list.tour.1.tabitem.single.realbrowser.monitor.right":"<div><h5>Take the user's path<\/h5><div>Test the availability, performance, and functionality of critical transactions in your website or web application, using a predefined set of user paths.<\/div><\/div>","mysql.metric.logbin.desc":"Log Bin","global.units.seconds":"seconds","practice.elb.without.multi.az.desc":"Elastic Load Balancer (ELB) nodes operating in a single Availability Zones are shown below.","lightsail.lb.title":"Lightsail Load Balancer","rum.add.mail":"Send Via Email","nsx.interface.received.errors":"Received Errors","global.s