eway.resource.path":"Resource Path","alibabacloud_rds_mysql.iofilemetrics":"I/O & File Metrics","direct.connect.connection.id":"Connection ID","reports.hyperv.vmvid.physicalpages":"Avg VM Vid Remote Physical Pages and Allocated Physical Pages","al.search.filter.placeholder":"Filter searches...","oci.opensearch.pipeline.otel.logs.request.timeouts":"OTEL Logs Request Timeouts","ncm.rule.severity.critical":"Critical","rum.analytics.campaign":"Campaign","plugin.app.sap_abap.report.min.enq.recent.lock.time.per.minute":"Min Recent Lock Time (Per Minute)","tp.client.test.selectmonitors.info":"Customize your test by associating multiple monitors from your existing monitor resource pool. You can either select all resources, manually pick relevant monitors from the list.","practice.azure.vm.multiple.eni.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks if the VM has multiple network interfaces attached.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p>Having multiple network interfaces on a VM can provide network redundancy and improve network performance. However, it can also increase complexity if their configurations are not similar. Resulting in performance differences, asymmetric traffic handling, inconsistency, and unpredictability, making it difficult to troubleshoot issues.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p>Verify if the VM needs to have more than one network interface card (NIC) attached to it and remove the unwanted NICs.<\/p>","rum.webvitals.needs.improvement":"Needs Improvement","report.time":"Time","cleanup.inactiveuser.mail.remainder2.content":"Dear {{n0}},\n \n As notified in the previous mail, your Site24x7 account remains inactive, and according to our data deletion policies, it will be cleaned up. \n \n We are reaching out to inform you that your Site24x7 account ({{n1}}) data will be deleted in 10 days.\n \n If you no longer wish to maintain your account and would like to have your data deleted, please disregard this email. We will proceed with the account clean-up and the deletion of all associated data. However, if you wish to retain your account and prevent the deletion of your data, please log in to \"https://www.site24x7.com\" and start monitoring. \n \n If you have any questions or require assistance, please reach out to our support team at support@site24x7.com.\n \n We appreciate your cooperation and look forward to continuing to serve you.\n \n Best regards,\n \n The Site24x7 team","digitalocean.monitor.add":"Add DigitalOcean Monitor","cl.nw.ucs.fabric_extender.switch.portsoper.statelinkup":"Fabric Extender Switch Portsoper Statelinkup","gcp.sa.impersonation":"Service Account Impersonation","amazon.elb.subnet":"SubnetId","rotation.details.heading.desc":"User groups associated with the shifts will be rotated periodically and alerts will be received accordingly.","alibabacloud_nlb.inactiveconnection":"Inactive Connections","predefined.report.7.description":"Detailed timing breakdown - DNS, connection, SSL, first byte, download","network.interface.discovery.time":"Discovery Time","problem.collapse":"Collapse","alibabacloud_apsaramq_kafka.instancemessagenumoutput":"Instance Message Num Output","glue.crawler.source.tables":"Tables Count","cl.nw.ucs.fabric.extender.serverPortstransportdce":"Server Ports Transport DCE","oci.fs.write.requests":"Write Requests","alibabacloud_ecs.sysommemmonreclaimpgscandirect":"Memory Reclaim Direct Page Scans","cl.nw.topn.interface.rx.errors.title":"Top 10 Interfaces by In Errors","aci.help.asstnt.com.terms.list6":"<strong>Endpoint Groups (EPGs):<\/strong> An endpoint is a single network device, connected to the network directly or indirectly. An EPG represents a group of endpoints, such as virtual machines, servers, or applications, that share common policy requirements.","azure.metric.materializedviewsbuilderaveragememoryusage.desc":"Materialized Views Builder Average Memory Usage","threshold.guardrails.intervention.rate.exceeds":"{{n0}} : Guardrails Intervention Rate {{n1}}%.","aws.rdspi.db.memory.manager.edit":"DB Memory Manager Edit","aci.help.asstnt.com.terms.list5":"<strong>Tenants:<\/strong> Within the ACI fabric, a tenant provides logical segmentation to isolate different sets of resources, such as networking, compute, and storage, while sharing the same physical infrastructure.","aci.help.asstnt.com.terms.list4":"<strong>Fabric:<\/strong> Comprises discrete components that are connected in a spine and leaf topology and managed as a single entity.","nutanix.virtual.disk.free.space.gib":"Free Space (GiB)","aci.help.asstnt.com.terms.list3":"<strong>Spine:<\/strong> Spine switches act as the backbone of the ACI fabric and help connect all the leaf nodes.","global.jsonschema.alert.severity.help.text":"Use the toggle button to set  the Alert Severity as DOWN or TROUBLE.<br><a href='{{help}}/admin/adding-a-monitor/rest-api-monitor.html#json' target='_blank'>Learn more.<\/a>","aws.dhcp.tags":"Tags Associated with DHCP Options Set","aci.help.asstnt.com.terms.list2":"<strong>Leaf:<\/strong> Access switches that aggregate traffic from servers and connect to the spine.","aci.help.asstnt.com.terms.list1":"<strong>Cisco Application Policy Infrastructure Controller:<\/strong> The main architectural component that is the unified point of automation and management for the Cisco ACI fabric.","azure.registry.chart.push.operations":"Push Operations","ec2.autoscaling.capacity.avg":"Average Desired Capacity","mobileapm.ios.header.swift":"In your AppDelegate.swift file, add the following statement:","oci.storage.bucket.object.event":"Object Events","sdn.arubacentral.tunnel.local.color":"Local Color","direct.connect.vlan":"VLAN","aws.cognito.idp.scopes":"Authorized scopes","server.update.plugin.module.info":"If disabled, Plugin Module will be removed from the server agent. Addition of Plugin Monitors will not be allowed for this server and data collection of existing plugin monitors in this server will be stopped.","global.ncm.discovery.poller.description":"Choose a