unt","errorcode.cause.cert.invalid":"Client certificate is invalid","kube.namespace.details":"Namespace Details","server.monitor.winupdate.step3":"Once installation is complete, the agent will auto-discover the Windows server and all the Windows updates.","usage.summary.purchase.addons":"To monitor {{n0}} monitors, users must <a ng-click=\"purchaseAddons({{n1}})\"> purchase {{n2}} <a> Monitor licenses.","practice.azure.disk.encrypt.with.cmk.info.desc":"<p><b>Baseline : <\/b><\/p><p>Checks whether the disk is encrypted with a customer-managed key (CMK) or Azure Disk Encryption.<\/p><p><b>Description : <\/b><\/p><p>Azure Managed Disks are encrypted by default at rest using server-side encryption (SSE) with platform managed keys (PMKs), which is storage-level encryption. Azure Key vault can be used to manage your own CMKs instead of using PMKs for encryption. CMKs provide enhanced control over encryption keys. ADE can also be used to encrypt managed disks using CMKs. Using platform-managed keys may not meet certain security and compliance requirements.<\/p><p><b>Recommendation : <\/b><\/p><p>Consider using SSE with CMK encryption or ADE for your managed disks to maintain control over the encryption keys and meet security requirements.<br>(<b>Note:<\/b> ADE is OS-level encryption when compared to SSE with CMKs, which is storage-level encryption (encryption at rest). Opt for ADE if strict OS-level compliance is needed else use SSE with CMK for general compliance. ADE can enabled for disks that are attached to the VM.<\/p>","azure.metric.ReimagingNodeCount.desc":"Number of reimaging nodes","update.hb.status":"You can use one of the below formats to push data from your endpoint(s)","scheduled.itautomation.daily.starttime.passed":"The it automation will be scheduled from tomorrow as today's Start Time set by you has already passed.","cl.nw.san.cifs.avg.directory.depth":"Avg Directory Depth","kube.node.conditions":"Conditions","max.container.iowrite":"Max I/O Write","hetzner