eport.avg.wp.upd2.total":"Avg U2 Work Processes Total","azure.resource.wvd.hosts.activeper":"Active Hosts Percent","al.fwd.name.required":"Name is required.","ec2.suggest.button.add":"Install the agent","aci.api.error.alert":"Alert when a connection to Cisco ACI API failed","tenant.details":"Tenant Details","aws.efs.title":"EFS","oci.compute.memoryEncryptionEnable":"Memory Encryption","cl.server.plugin.dep.empty":"No Plugin Deployments added","query.check.evaluation.mode":"Evaluation Mode","practice.ses.dkim.enabled":"Amazon SES - DKIM signature","server.disk.valid.threshold":"Enter a valid Disk Utilization threshold value","alibabacloud_rds.pg_proxycpuutilization":"PostgreSQL Proxy CPU Utilization","aws.fsx.svm.volume.style.chart":"Volume count based on Volume Style","dashboards.write.requests":"Dashboards Write Requests per Minute per Project","network.help.discoverdevice.pt1":"<ul><li><a ng-click=\"addDataToMics(constants.network.mics_tracker.help_asst_device)\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-label=\"click here to go to the Network Discovery page.\" href=\"#/network/network-discovery/DEVICE\">Click here<\/a> to go to the Network Discovery page.<\/li><li>Type either the IP Address or the Device Name of the device to be discovered.<\/li><li>Select the On-Premise poller which you want to use for this Monitor.<\/li><li>Select the discovery credentials.<\/li><li>Click <strong>Add Device<\/strong> to add a Device.<\/li><li>Go to <strong>Network Devices<\/strong> page to view the added network devices.<\/li><\/ul>","practice.gcp.iam.service.account.admin.access.desc":"Identifies principals with service account user or token creator roles.","gcporg.tab.allprojects":"All Projects","aws.rds.proxy.database.connections.currently.session.pinned":"Database Connections Currently Session Pinned","digitalocean_uptime.summary.title":"Summary Title","tools.share.this":"Share This","azure.metric.jobscreateDirectMethodJobfailure.disp":"Failed creations of method invocation jobs","mongodbatlas.cachefillratio":"Cache Fill Ratio","alibabacloud_oss.InternetRecvBandwidthUsageRate":"Internet Recv Bandwidth Usage Rate","azure.metric.tomcatglobalerror.desc":"Tomcat Global Error","report.apm.top.bg.transactions.by.avg.resp.time":"Average Background Transactions by Response time","kube.nw.monitoring.enable":"Enable Network Monitoring","dbinsight.cpuq.groupby.title":"CPU Intensive Queries Statistics","subscriptions.additonal.alerts.2500":"2500 Additional Alert Credits","azure.metric.Runs.disp":"Agent Runs","tfa.disable.push.notification":"Please authorize this action to disable Two-Factor Authentication for time-sensitive operations.","aws.endpoint.max.count.threshold.title":"Endpoints Connections Threshold","global.subtitle.textratio":"Text Ratio","rdspi.db.sql.stats.execution.plan.count":"Execution Plan Count","alibabacloud_ehpc.queuedjobs":"Queued Jobs","mail.presales.activity.free.content.1":"<p>Hello,<\/p><p>Take another look at our Next Gen Site24x7- Nothing like what you saw before.<\/p><p>By combining in one view Web performance monitoring information from your user&#39;s perspective, key performance indicators across datacenter and cloud infrastructure, and deep application code visibility, life for IT Operations teams across SMBs and Enterprises can get much easier!<\/p><p><span style=\"padding-left:80px; padding-right:70px;\"><a href=\"https://{{n1}}/application-performance-monitoring.html\"><img src=\"cid:image.part.presalesimage\"><\/a><\/span><br>Choose Site24x7 to identify and resolve performance degradation no matter where they originate.<p>{{n0}}","plugin.app.sap_abap.report.min.wp.enq.total":"Min Enqueue Work Processes Total","kube.vm.livemigratable":"Live Migratable","mail.presales.activity.free.content.3":"<p>Hello,<\/p><p>Web user experience can be severely impacted by underperforming app code. Isolate the culprit now! Site24x7 APM Insight gives you deep code-level visibility into how your applications behave end-to-end, from URL to SQL query.<\/p><p>Here are some tips to help you get started with Site24x7 APM Insight evaluation<br> <b>1. Download Site24x7 APM Insight agent<\/b><br><b>2. Deploy it in your application instances<\/b><br><b>3. Automatically collect deep code-level information across Java, .NET or Ruby applications<\/b><\/p><p>Developers can now fix slow web transactions and get detailed performance metrics by looking into:<ul><li>Transaction Traces<\/li><li>Database Response Time by Operation<\/li><li>Underperforming methods<\/li><li>Application response time broken by tier<\/li><li>Application Throughput<\/li><li>End-User Satisfaction (Apdex Scores) and more<\/li> <\/ul><\/p><span style=\"padding-left:50px; padding-right:50px;\"><img src=\"cid:image.part.presalesimage\"><\/span>Get never before insight into your application performance end-to-end. For more on how the installation works, visit the <a href=\"{{n2}}help/admin/adding-a-monitor.html\">help center<\/a>.<p>{{n0}}","mail.presales.activity.free.content.2":"<p>Hello,<\/p><p>User experience will be negatively impacted if your cloud infrastructure underperforms.  Did you know that Site24x7&#39;s Pro Plan and above now gives you complete visibility into cloud/virtual resources, on the same console you already use?<\/p> <p><b>Getting started with Site24x7 Public and Private Cloud Monitoring<\/b><\/p><p>1. Configure VMware Monitors and alerting policies- <a href=\"https://help.site24x7.com/configuring-site24x7-vmware-monitors.html\">See how<\/a><br>2. Configure Amazon Monitors and alerting policies- <a href=\"https://help.site24x7.com/monitor-amazon-cloud.html#configure new aws monitor\">See how<\/a><br><span style=\"padding-left:50px; padding-right:50px;\"><img src=\"cid:image.part.presalesimage\"><\/span><p>3. Automatically track key performance indicators including: <ul><li>Availability, CPU Utilization and Disk Utilization across virtual machines<\/li><li>Hardware (power, fan)<\/li><li>EC2 instances (availability, CPU, network in)<\/li><li>RDS Instances (read/write latency, read/write throughput, CPU, database connections, availability)<\/li><li>S3 Buckets (name, location, creation time, size, number of objects and virtual folders)<\/li><li>SNS Topics (Number of messages published, publish size, number of notifications delivered and failed)<\/li> <li>DynamoDB Tables (Throttling, Latency and Error metrics)<\/li><li>Lambda Functions (Invocations, Duration, Errors and Throttles)<\/li><\/ul>With Site24x7 you will know that virtualized and cloud resources are functioning at peak performance and even monitor, verify and demonstrate if SLAs are being met.<\/p><p>{{n0}}","client.marketing.lambda.noresource":"Oops, looks like there are no monitored Lambda Functions. This may be because of one or more of the following reasons:","alibabacloud_mongodb.transtotalpreparedps":"Transactions Total Prepared Per Second","home.monitors.list.tour.1.addiconsitem.global.monitors.right":"<div><h5>Keep adding monitors<\/h5><div>Add your preferred monitors and monitor types using the + button.<\/div><\/div>","huaweicloud_bms.tab.NPU":"NPU","alibabacloud_acs_ksm.code5xx1m":"Code 5xx 1M","alibabacloud_fc.functionqualifiermemorylimitmb":"Function Qualifier Memory Limit (MB)","global.action.hyperv.mem.dynamic":"Enable Dynamic Memory","glue.trigger.deactive":"Deactive Triggers","aws.agentcore.codeinterpreter.cpu.vcpu.hours":"CPU (vCPU-Hours)","sdn.citrixSdwan.customer.side.tab.title":"Citrix SD-WAN Customer","alibabacloud_analyticsdb_mysql.insertinbytes":"Insert In Bytes","of365.threshold.accountsdisabled.exceeds":"Account disabled exceeds","network.action":"Settings","apminsight.recent.five.exception.traces":"Recent 5 Exception Traces","global.multiple.website.defacement.monitor":"Website Defacement Monitor(s)","add.alibabacloud_ecs.monitor":"Add Alibaba Cloud ECS Monitor","practice.azure.loadbalancer.orphan.desc":"You could either utilise the Load Balancer(s) or delete them.","azure.metric.noconns.desc":"Total Number of Conn