evice.ups.lastselftestresult":"Last self-test Date","azure.resource.postgresql.promptlabel":"PostgreSQL Database","nsx.lb.virtual.server.capacity":"Virtual Server Capacity","advanced.threshold.conf.info":"<p>In Advanced Threshold Configuration, you can create complex conditions by combining multiple thresholds to receive customized alerts. Here's how it works:<p><ul><li><b>Logical Operators:<\/b> Use && (AND) to require all conditions to be met, or || (OR) to trigger an alert if any condition is met.<\/li><li><b>Attribute Grouping:<\/b> Use parentheses ( ) to group thresholds and control the evaluation order, allowing for precise combinations.<\/li><li><b>Conditions:<\/b> You can create one each of three conditions---Critical, Down, and Trouble. For each condition, you can configure up to ten thresholds to customize your alerts.<\/li><li><b>Threshold Validation:<\/b> Each attribute can have conditions like >, <, >=, or <= to determine if it meets the alert criteria.<\/li><\/ul><p>By using these advanced rules, you can customize your alerting system for complex scenarios, ensuring alerts are sent only when necessary.<\/p>","k8s.pd.overview.discovery.state":"Discovery state","velocloud.handoff.queue.drops":"Handoff Queue Drops","alerts.sms.number.format":"Format","dynamodb.threshold.throttled.batch.get.itm.req":"Throttled BatchGetItem requests","reports.topn.azapi.computesize":"API Management service by Compute Size","rds.backup.retention.storage":"Backup Retention Period Storage Used","ec2.cpucreditbalance.graph.yaxislabel.text":"CPU Credit Balance Count","confirm.show.all.config":"Show all unchanged configurations","apminsight.flowmap.zohologs":"Zoho Logs","server.inventory.biz.msg.box":"Message Box Database","cl.nw.ucs.server_interface.link.state":"Server Interface Link State","client.marketing.oci.nosql.bullet2":"You have opted out of monitoring by unselecting the checkbox next to the OCI NoSQL listing.","alibabacloud_nas.hw_appliance_power":"HW Appliance Power","